---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "The Long Road — The Geriatrician's Guide";
const description = "A guide to senior living decisions written by a Stanford-trained geriatrician. One book for all stages.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="wrap section">

    <div class="product-hero">
      <div class="product-hero__text">
        <p class="eyebrow">Flagship Guide</p>
        <h1 class="product-hero__title">The Long Road</h1>
        <p class="product-hero__sub">The guidance a geriatrician gives when no one&rsquo;s paying him to steer you &mdash; from the first worrying signs through touring, memory care, and hospice. What to ask, what each choice really costs, and how to decide with confidence instead of guilt.</p>
        <p class="product-hero__price">$97 <span class="product-hero__price-note">one-time payment</span></p>
        <!-- LEMON SQUEEZY PRODUCT URL HERE -->
        <a class="btn btn--accent" href="#">Get Instant Access
          <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="product-hero__figure">
        <img src="/images/the-long-road-cover.png" alt="The Long Road — A Geriatrician's Complete Guide to Senior Care Decisions, by Michael D. Genualdi, MD" width="2474" height="3200" />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="book-org" style="margin-top:56px">
      <h2 class="section-head">How the book is organized</h2>
      <div class="book-stats">
        <div class="book-stat"><span class="book-stat__num">6</span><span class="book-stat__label">Parts</span></div>
        <div class="book-stat"><span class="book-stat__num">41</span><span class="book-stat__label">Chapters</span></div>
        <div class="book-stat"><span class="book-stat__num">1</span><span class="book-stat__label">Book for all stages</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="book-org__note">Written to be read out of order. Every chapter opens with what it answers, who it&rsquo;s for, and when you need it &mdash; and closes with one action worth taking this week. Start at the stage you&rsquo;re in.</p>

      <ol class="parts-list">
        <li class="part-row">
          <div class="part-row__rail"><span class="part-row__num">I</span><span class="part-row__ch">Ch. 1&ndash;10</span></div>
          <div class="part-row__body">
            <h3 class="part-row__title">Before the Decision</h3>
            <p class="part-row__desc">Telling worrying from unsafe, how much time you actually have, the levels of care, raising it with a parent who refuses &mdash; and the legal documents that have to exist before a crisis.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="part-row">
          <div class="part-row__rail"><span class="part-row__num">II</span><span class="part-row__ch">Ch. 11&ndash;18</span></div>
          <div class="part-row__body">
            <h3 class="part-row__title">The Financial Picture</h3>
            <p class="part-row__desc">What care actually costs and how to pay for it: care-tier pricing, Medicare vs. Medicaid, long-term care insurance, veterans benefits, the house, and a funding plan that lasts.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="part-row">
          <div class="part-row__rail"><span class="part-row__num">III</span><span class="part-row__ch">Ch. 19&ndash;21</span></div>
          <div class="part-row__body">
            <h3 class="part-row__title">Choosing Well: Touring, Evaluating, and Deciding</h3>
            <p class="part-row__desc">Touring past the staging, reading what the tour leaves out, and understanding the contract and care plan before you sign.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="part-row">
          <div class="part-row__rail"><span class="part-row__num">IV</span><span class="part-row__ch">Ch. 22&ndash;30</span></div>
          <div class="part-row__body">
            <h3 class="part-row__title">After Move-In: Staying Involved</h3>
            <p class="part-row__desc">The first 90 days, who manages medical care now, reading a care plan, medication safety, monitoring from a distance, hospitalizations and the risky return, and spotting neglect.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="part-row">
          <div class="part-row__rail"><span class="part-row__num">V</span><span class="part-row__ch">Ch. 31&ndash;36</span></div>
          <div class="part-row__body">
            <h3 class="part-row__title">Dementia: Understanding, Caring, and Deciding</h3>
            <p class="part-row__desc">The types and stages, why behaviors happen and how to respond, staying connected as the person changes, choosing memory care, and planning for an end they may not be able to choose.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="part-row">
          <div class="part-row__rail"><span class="part-row__num">VI</span><span class="part-row__ch">Ch. 37&ndash;40</span></div>
          <div class="part-row__body">
            <h3 class="part-row__title">The End of Life</h3>
            <p class="part-row__desc">The goals-of-care conversation, palliative care vs. hospice, how hospice works inside a community, and what a good death looks like &mdash; and how to advocate for it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-head" style="margin-top:56px">What&rsquo;s inside</h2>
    <ul class="whats-inside">
      <li>What senior living actually costs &mdash; the base rate on the brochure, the care-level fees no one volunteers on the tour, and how a manageable number climbs to thousands more, faster than most people plan for.</li>
      <li>Whether you have three weeks or six months to decide &mdash; and how to tell the difference, so a single bad afternoon doesn&rsquo;t force the choice before you&rsquo;re ready.</li>
      <li>The exact wording that keeps the door open when you&rsquo;re met with resistance &mdash; and the phrasing that, without meaning to, slams it shut.</li>
      <li>How to find the public safety record most people never check before touring &mdash; who owns a community, and what that means for staffing and care.</li>
      <li>Exactly which questions to ask on a tour, and how to read the answer. A confident community gives you a straight answer; a practiced non-answer is itself information.</li>
      <li>The contract clauses that matter most: the escalation clause with no real ceiling, and the discharge language that decides who gets to stay as things get harder.</li>
      <li>How to evaluate a memory care unit like a clinician &mdash; why the people on shift, not the locked door, are the real safety mechanism.</li>
      <li>Why the days after a hospital discharge are the riskiest stretch in the entire process &mdash; and the two things that decide whether a community takes someone back.</li>
      <li>The medication risk hiding in plain sight, one reasonable addition at a time &mdash; and how to make sure every drug your loved one takes still has a reason.</li>
      <li>What happens at the end, and how hospice works &mdash; so you know what to expect and how to advocate for someone who no longer can.</li>
      <li>How to keep doing this without it taking you down too &mdash; respite, paid help, and the permission most caregivers never give themselves.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="free-chapter" style="margin-top:48px">
      <p>Not sure yet? Read a free chapter before you buy.</p>
      <p class="fc__sub">Enter your email, confirm it, and the chapter arrives in your inbox.<br>No spam, no placement calls. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
      <!-- Kit form 9942260 — posts to Kit, which tags the subscriber and fires the incentive email with the chapter PDF. -->
      <form class="email-form email-form--dark" id="fc-form" action="https://app.kit.com/forms/9942260/subscriptions" method="post">
        <input type="email" name="email_address" placeholder="you@email.com" aria-label="Email address" required>
        <button type="submit">Send me the chapter</button>
      </form>
      <p class="fc__fine" id="fc-fine">We never sell your personal information.</p>
      <p class="fc__done" id="fc-done" hidden>Check your inbox &mdash; click the confirmation link and the chapter is on its way.</p>
    </div>


  </div>


<script is:inline>
    var fc=document.getElementById('fc-form');if(fc){fc.addEventListener('submit',function(e){e.preventDefault();window.ggKitSubmit(fc,function(){fc.hidden=true;document.getElementById('fc-fine').hidden=true;document.getElementById('fc-done').hidden=false;});});}
</script>
</BaseLayout>
